        "original_id": "eb982bfb-9422-5858-8ac9-041e5a3b39c2",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Jean Vander Pyl\n- Works: The Jetsons, Top Cat, The Secret Squirrel Show, The Magilla Gorilla Show, The Funtastic World of Hanna-Barbera\n- Characters: Wilma Flintstone, Pebbles Flintstone, Rosie, Goldie, Lola Glamour, Nurse LaRue, Winsome Witch, Ogee\n- Companies: Hanna-Barbera\n\nFacts:\n- The Jetsons is an American animated sitcom produced by Hanna-Barbera.\n- The Jetsons originally aired in primetime from September 23, 1962, to March 17, 1963.\n- Jean Vander Pyl voiced Wilma Flintstone and also voiced Pebbles Flintstone.\n- Jean Vander Pyl voiced Rosie the robot maid on The Jetsons.\n- Jean Vander Pyl voiced Goldie, Lola Glamour, Nurse LaRue, and other characters in Top Cat.\n- Jean Vander Pyl voiced Winsome Witch on The Secret Squirrel Show.\n- Jean Vander Pyl voiced Ogee on The Magilla Gorilla Show.\n- The Jetsons later aired in syndication, with new episodes from 1985 to 1987 as part of The Funtastic World of Hanna-Barbera block.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "7a916a4c-263b-5bfa-b257-9b1e8bc84d21",
        "text": "Page: Jean Vander Pyl. Sentence: In addition to Wilma Flintstone, she also provided the voices of Pebbles Flintstone, Rosie the robot maid on the animated series \"The Jetsons\", Goldie, Lola Glamour, Nurse LaRue and other characters in \"Top Cat\", Winsome Witch on \"The Secret Squirrel Show\" and Ogee on \"The Magilla Gorilla Show\".\nPage: The Jetsons. Sentence: The Jetsons is an American animated sitcom produced by Hanna-Barbera, originally airing in primetime from September 23, 1962, to March 17, 1963, then later in syndication, with new episodes in 1985 to 1987 as part of \"The Funtastic World of Hanna-Barbera\" block.",
